WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:03.270
<b>KEEP OUT</b>

00:03.270 --> 00:06.230
<b>POLICE</b>

00:04.960 --> 00:07.790
You'd better have a good 
explanation for all this.

00:09.520 --> 00:13.150
First, could we have some privacy?

00:17.340 --> 00:19.790
I could've sworn they didn't 
give themselves away.

00:19.790 --> 00:21.750
Can you see through walls or something?

00:22.010 --> 00:24.710
That's part of what I have to tell you.

00:26.160 --> 00:27.610
Hey! You heard the man!

00:27.610 --> 00:29.050
But... Your Lordship—

00:29.050 --> 00:30.330
Beat it!

00:35.120 --> 00:38.810
I'm pretty sure they're all gone.
Now, you were saying?

00:39.600 --> 00:40.600
Well, sir...

00:42.130 --> 00:44.060
I don't expect you to believe me,

00:44.730 --> 00:47.370
but I'm not from this world.

02:20.010 --> 02:22.580
Well done, Nezu.

02:23.210 --> 02:24.450
I'm grateful.

02:25.750 --> 02:27.180
Hm? What is it?

02:30.930 --> 02:33.500
Polka reached the twins before you did?

02:35.210 --> 02:38.620
Would you care to elaborate on that?

02:41.050 --> 02:42.430
I see.

02:42.430 --> 02:45.640
That's certainly a hard pill to swallow.

02:45.640 --> 02:48.250
But after what I've seen, well...

02:49.270 --> 02:51.230
Now, then.

02:51.230 --> 02:53.310
Based on what you just told me,

02:55.800 --> 02:59.960
it sounds like <i>you</i> slit 
Polka's throat, young lady.

03:00.870 --> 03:02.930
Yup. That's true.

03:02.930 --> 03:05.660
Admitting that to my face takes guts.

03:05.900 --> 03:08.870
Are you prepared for a messy death?

03:08.870 --> 03:12.940
Or are you trying to show 
you're not afraid of me?

03:16.370 --> 03:19.100
Well... both, I guess.

03:20.560 --> 03:23.370
You're a good person, so you don't scare me.

03:23.890 --> 03:26.780
And I figure I can't 
complain if you kill me.

03:29.020 --> 03:31.230
<b>Wait, Dad!
Don't kill her!</b>

03:29.370 --> 03:31.230
Whoa! What the hell?!

03:33.810 --> 03:37.200
Wait, Dad! Don't kill Shiro!

03:40.650 --> 03:43.430
Are you... Polka?

03:43.430 --> 03:44.370
What?!

03:44.050 --> 03:45.820
<b>NOD NOD</b>

03:45.820 --> 03:48.490
You said his soul is safe.

03:48.490 --> 03:51.290
Does this mean he's not 
asleep inside his body?

03:51.710 --> 03:54.170
<b>NOD NOD</b>

03:51.710 --> 03:54.170
<b>Shark Metronome</b>

03:51.710 --> 03:54.170

m 0 0 l 150 0 150 25 0 25

03:54.170 --> 03:57.840
<b>Pretty cool, huh?</b>

03:54.410 --> 03:57.840
Why the Sharkborg From Hell, of all things?

04:00.550 --> 04:03.230
Well, this is only temporary, so...

04:06.740 --> 04:08.580
Damn it, that was a low blow!

04:08.580 --> 04:13.020
And to top it all off, 
Polka seems to <i>like</i> it!

04:13.020 --> 04:15.840
How am I supposed to stay mad?!

04:16.440 --> 04:19.190
Still, if you think <i>I'm</i> a good person,

04:19.190 --> 04:22.150
you need your eyes checked, missy.

04:23.420 --> 04:26.070
Oh, well. Where were we?

04:26.620 --> 04:29.950
You, the... Corpse God? Is that it?

04:30.350 --> 04:34.980
You can turn Polka back to normal as long 
as you've got another body to possess.

04:35.690 --> 04:39.670
In that case, I wouldn't mind 
hooking you up with one of these.

04:39.970 --> 04:42.000
<i>What an exquisite golem.</i>

04:42.000 --> 04:44.650
<i>There were experiments 
with them in my homeland,</i>

04:44.650 --> 04:46.150
<i>but this is quite—</i>

04:47.090 --> 04:49.560
<b>TAP TAP TAP</b>

04:49.560 --> 04:52.730
What? If one of us becomes a robot,
you want it to be you?

04:52.730 --> 04:55.930
No. What would be the point 
of <i>you</i> possessing it?

04:55.930 --> 04:58.230
You also want a rock drill 
and the power of flight?

04:58.230 --> 04:59.820
Why do you want mining equipment?

04:59.820 --> 05:05.330
Well, he seems... I can't say <i>healthy</i>, 
but I'm glad he's not suffering.

05:05.850 --> 05:09.280
Anyway, if someone is out to kill Polka,

05:09.490 --> 05:12.750
he should be safer with you in his body.

05:12.750 --> 05:13.730
Then...

05:13.730 --> 05:15.330
Don't get me wrong.

05:15.330 --> 05:18.290
I haven't let this young lady off the hook.

05:18.550 --> 05:22.200
But she did save two of my grandkids.

05:31.110 --> 05:32.350
Whelp.

05:33.210 --> 05:36.600
I didn't press for details 
about their "intermediary,"

05:36.870 --> 05:40.950
but they mentioned Shinjuku,
so it's probably the Kuraki girl.

05:40.950 --> 05:45.780
She's got heavy hitters in her corner,
so I'd rather avoid a fight.

05:45.990 --> 05:50.370
And I don't want to believe anyone 
in my family would go after Polka...

05:51.290 --> 05:52.330
But...

05:53.080 --> 05:55.640
Well, I guess that's my karma 
catching up to me.

05:57.700 --> 06:01.630
So, we'll leave once we look 
in on the real Polka's pet.

06:01.630 --> 06:04.510
<i>Wait, you actually told them?</i>

06:04.740 --> 06:06.880
<i>Yes, but only Rozan-san.</i>

06:06.900 --> 06:09.860
<i>My textbooks... 
My game consoles...</i>

06:07.200 --> 06:09.980
<i>Well, I guess it's your call.</i>

06:09.980 --> 06:12.570
I got permission to live in 
Shinjuku for the time being.

06:14.940 --> 06:19.730
Um... I know it's too late for an apology,

06:19.730 --> 06:21.360
but I'll say this anyway.

06:21.820 --> 06:22.750
Sorry.

06:23.800 --> 06:26.210
And thanks.

06:29.610 --> 06:32.280
<i></i>Don't worry about it.

06:30.870 --> 06:32.280
<i>That's unusual.</i>

06:32.950 --> 06:36.620
<i>Not many souls are so open 
with their murderers.</i>

06:37.800 --> 06:39.290
<i>The last one I met was...</i>

06:40.420 --> 06:43.660
W-Wait up! Misaki-oneechan!

06:47.110 --> 06:48.860
Uh... Um...

06:49.840 --> 06:52.550
Thanks... for saving us.

06:54.010 --> 06:59.170
E-Earlier, well, we were scared, but...

07:00.990 --> 07:02.290
Don't sweat it.

07:02.290 --> 07:05.440
You kids wouldn't live long 
if that <i>didn't</i> freak you out.

07:05.890 --> 07:08.890
Are you a martial artist?

07:08.890 --> 07:10.110
I'm not telling!

07:11.230 --> 07:13.670
E-Excuse me! Uncle Polka!

07:14.810 --> 07:17.540
Thank you... very much.

07:18.430 --> 07:19.580
Thank you.

07:19.960 --> 07:22.170
I'm not the one you 
should be thanking.

07:22.390 --> 07:25.130
I didn't come to your rescue earlier.

07:25.360 --> 07:28.740
That was a fortune teller from 
Shinjuku called the Corpse God,

07:28.740 --> 07:30.590
along with your guardian spirit.

07:33.380 --> 07:35.870
I can't see any spirit, but what's the plan?

07:35.870 --> 07:38.810
Are you gonna make a contract with her?

07:39.850 --> 07:43.270
Eventually, but not now.

07:50.180 --> 07:52.440
It's not time yet.

07:53.570 --> 07:56.660
<i>Tokyo
 Detention
 House</i>

07:53.940 --> 07:56.660
I just heard from the station.

07:56.660 --> 07:59.220
The <i>real</i> Fire-Breathing Bug showed up.

07:59.750 --> 08:02.520
Really? What impeccable timing.

08:03.200 --> 08:04.130
What's the damage?

08:04.450 --> 08:08.050
The fire took out one patrol car and 
the arsonist it was transporting.

08:09.130 --> 08:12.380
The Bug merely preyed on its imitator.

08:12.380 --> 08:16.720
I find those skeletons far more intriguing.

08:16.720 --> 08:20.430
Would you mind giving me 
another look at the video?

08:20.430 --> 08:23.770
Sorry, but if you want more, 
you'll have to trade info for it.

08:23.770 --> 08:26.650
I see. What a shame.

08:27.660 --> 08:30.580
In that case, I'll go see for myself.

08:33.040 --> 08:33.850
Here.

08:33.850 --> 08:35.990
Oh, hey. You came prepared.

08:35.990 --> 08:38.330
That mess at the club taught me a le—

08:40.330 --> 08:42.290
You've gotta be kidding me.

08:42.720 --> 08:46.120
I planned for a lot, but not for <i>this</i>...

08:46.120 --> 08:48.520
<i></i>Tokyo
Detention
House

08:46.120 --> 08:48.540
Phantom Solitaire!

08:48.750 --> 08:53.110
Now, it's time for Ten'a Sorimura
to stage a comeback.

08:54.020 --> 08:58.180
If no one comes to watch, I'll just 
have to sob alone in the moonlit night.

09:01.010 --> 09:05.520
<b></b>Well, it
<i>is</i> white...

09:01.660 --> 09:05.520
It's Shiro! What a big cutie-pie!

09:05.770 --> 09:09.530
<i>The real Polka is no slouch.</i>

09:11.480 --> 09:14.740
Investigation Report

09:11.480 --> 09:14.740
<b>Ten'a Sorimura</b>

09:12.810 --> 09:14.740
The Phantom Solitaire

09:14.740 --> 09:19.210
escaped from Tokyo Detention House 
at approximately 5:30 p.m. today.

09:14.740 --> 09:20.280
EMERGENCY MEETING!!

09:19.210 --> 09:20.280
E-Excuse me, sir?

09:20.720 --> 09:24.480
I thought you and Arase-san 
went there to question him.

09:24.480 --> 09:28.070
We did! He up and vanished in 
the middle of our interview!

09:28.070 --> 09:29.780
It was timed like a practical joke!

09:29.770 --> 09:31.590
<b>HEE
HEE
HEE...</b>

09:29.780 --> 09:31.590
Seriously? That's hilarious.

09:31.590 --> 09:33.340
It's not funny.

09:31.590 --> 09:36.800
EMERGENCY MEETING!!

09:33.340 --> 09:36.800
For us, at least, it's not funny in the least!

09:36.800 --> 09:39.800
He started causing trouble three years ago

09:40.060 --> 09:43.930
when he stole a painting from a museum 
and left it outside Alta in Shinjuku.

09:44.250 --> 09:48.400
His motive was that he "wanted to 
give Shinjuku's YouTubers a scoop."

09:48.700 --> 09:50.560
His next crime

09:50.730 --> 09:53.340
was making the Metropolitan 
Government Building disappear.

09:53.340 --> 09:56.980
In one night, he covered it in pictures 
of the sky and other buildings,

09:56.980 --> 10:01.180
using trick art to make it look 
like the whole place had vanished.

10:01.180 --> 10:04.540
We think he was also behind 
a long list of other crimes,

10:04.540 --> 10:09.460
<b><i></i>Teleporting jumbo jet!</b>

10:04.540 --> 10:09.460
<b><i></i>Shinjuku dream fireworks!</b>

10:04.540 --> 10:09.460
<b><i></i>Disappearing
government building!</b>

10:04.540 --> 10:09.460
<b>Shinjuku</b>

10:04.540 --> 10:09.460
including suspected murders, but we 
don't have enough to pin those on him.

10:09.690 --> 10:13.420
Then came the case that 
made him world-famous.

10:13.420 --> 10:16.380
Kidnapping the prime minister?

10:16.380 --> 10:17.540
Exactly.

10:17.540 --> 10:22.810
A black cloth was suddenly dropped onto 
Prime Minister Yumenosuke Kubikigawara.

10:22.810 --> 10:27.600
When his panicked security pulled it off,
he was gone without a trace.

10:27.600 --> 10:30.520
<i>Ladies and gentlemen! I commit 
crimes for the thrill!</i>

10:30.520 --> 10:33.570
<i>I do not endorse any political ideology!</i>

10:33.570 --> 10:36.030
<i>And today, I'll prove it to you!</i>

10:36.680 --> 10:43.060
Then, for one day, he abducted the heads 
of all the opposition parties, too.

10:42.570 --> 10:49.430
m 0 0 l 200 0 200 25 0 25

10:42.570 --> 10:49.430
<b><i>SCOOP!</i></b>

10:42.570 --> 10:49.430
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 20 0 20</b>

10:42.570 --> 10:49.430
<b>PM: "It was a blast."</b>

10:42.570 --> 10:49.430
m 0 0 l 450 0 450 55 0 55

10:43.060 --> 10:45.430
When the PM was released 
that evening, he said:

10:45.430 --> 10:48.910
"The next thing I knew, I was in 
a manga cafe reading <i>Murciélago</i>."

10:50.130 --> 10:52.560
He added, "It was a blast,"

10:52.560 --> 10:56.880
but we don't know if he meant 
the manga or the kidnapping.

10:56.880 --> 11:02.090
<b>That's crazy 
funny~</b>

10:57.400 --> 11:02.090
Inevitably, Japanese security became 
an international laughingstock.

11:02.330 --> 11:05.060
Then Solitaire turned himself in.

11:05.590 --> 11:08.350
And, to no one's surprise, 
he had a screw lose.

11:09.050 --> 11:11.060
What brought this on?

11:11.450 --> 11:14.610
Audience indifference got 
to be too much for me.

11:14.610 --> 11:17.650
What? Everyone's talking about you.

11:17.650 --> 11:19.110
I don't mean <i>them</i>.

11:19.430 --> 11:23.570
I wanted to use my magic 
to hoodwink the real thing.

11:23.860 --> 11:24.930
What do you mean?

11:24.930 --> 11:27.430
I perform tricks and illusions,

11:27.430 --> 11:31.520
but I believe that the 
fantastic does truly exist.

11:31.520 --> 11:37.490
My crimes are a message to those 
genuine sorcerers and psychics!

11:37.490 --> 11:43.110
If one of them reaches out to me as 
a fellow wizard, I'll have proof!

11:43.110 --> 11:48.720
Proof that there is such a thing 
as magic with no trick behind it!

11:49.630 --> 11:55.250
What?! You disturbed the whole 
country for that childish crap?

11:55.250 --> 12:00.110
A dreaming child lives inside 
each and every one of us.

12:00.110 --> 12:04.840
I looked at those imaginary 
children and thought to myself:

12:04.840 --> 12:09.150
How free and pure they are!

12:09.150 --> 12:13.830
As a responsible adult, 
I'll make their dreams come true!

12:13.830 --> 12:17.790
And I don't care if I become a 
criminal and a nuisance to do it!

12:18.600 --> 12:19.760
I see.

12:20.360 --> 12:21.340
Restrain him.

12:22.260 --> 12:24.230
Have you forgotten your childhood dreams?!

12:24.230 --> 12:25.080
Shut up!

12:24.630 --> 12:29.500
I don't know how much of his last speech 
was true and how much was bullshit.

12:25.880 --> 12:28.650
Take that! Mysterious pellet!

12:27.300 --> 12:30.770
<b>Shinjuku 
Police Station</b>

12:30.770 --> 12:36.980
EMERGENCY MEETING!!

12:30.770 --> 12:37.580
His technique and energy are superhuman, 
but that's not the worst thing about him.

12:36.980 --> 12:40.420
<b>Ten'a Sorimura</b>

12:38.080 --> 12:39.830
Not even close.

12:42.240 --> 12:43.380
What's this?

12:43.380 --> 12:44.990
A modern convenience.

12:44.990 --> 12:48.890
I bought it in a secondhand shop 
on that street for 2,000 yen.

12:46.050 --> 12:50.830
Corpse God, thou
 hast found a radio!

12:46.050 --> 12:50.830
m 0 0 l 150 0 150 60 0 60

12:48.470 --> 12:50.830
Money:

20,000 yen
→
18,000 yen

12:48.470 --> 12:50.830
m 0 0 l 90 0 90 100 0 100

12:48.890 --> 12:50.830
It will help me gather intelligence.

12:51.090 --> 12:54.650
Y'know, with 20 grand, you could 
at least afford a cheap tablet.

12:53.640 --> 12:55.920
<b><i>My dress
is ruined...</i></b>

12:58.680 --> 13:00.590
<i>And now, our next story.</i>

13:00.590 --> 13:02.170
Ooh.

13:02.170 --> 13:03.900
<i>A police vehicle caught fire this afternoon,</i>

13:02.170 --> 13:04.130
The sound works.

13:03.900 --> 13:07.250
<i>resulting in the confirmed death 
of one suspect it was transporting.</i>

13:07.960 --> 13:12.600
<i>The suspect, an unidentified male, 
was arrested for suspected arson.</i>

13:12.600 --> 13:13.410
What?

13:12.600 --> 13:15.440
<i>Police are currently working to identify him.</i>

13:13.410 --> 13:15.060
You've gotta be kidding me.

13:15.440 --> 13:18.240
That's the guy who tried 
to torch the Shinoyamas.

13:19.670 --> 13:21.270
<i>And now, more breaking news.</i>

13:21.630 --> 13:25.660
<i>Do you all remember a man 
named Ten'a Sorimura?</i>

13:25.660 --> 13:26.820
Goodness gracious!

13:25.720 --> 13:31.280
<b>25-Year Shinjuku
Precinct Veteran

Fumiyo Yamada</b>

13:25.720 --> 13:31.280
<b>m 0 0 l 150 0 150 75 0 75</b>

13:27.060 --> 13:31.280
Tsubaki-chan! Everyone! Look what's on TV!

13:31.280 --> 13:32.790
Who's Tsubaki-chan?

13:32.790 --> 13:35.500
That's Inspector Iwanome's first name.

13:35.770 --> 13:37.120
What's up?

13:37.120 --> 13:38.210
Quick! Check the TV!

13:38.210 --> 13:41.400
<b>Public Nuisance Escapes!!</b>

13:38.440 --> 13:41.420
They're reporting on Solitaire's escape!

13:41.710 --> 13:42.550
What?!

13:42.870 --> 13:44.550
Didn't you impose media restrictions?

13:44.550 --> 13:45.510
I sure thought I did!

13:45.510 --> 13:50.250
<i>This handsome fellow swiftly committed 
and solved the crime of the century</i>

13:45.510 --> 13:54.740
<b>Public nuisance escapes</b>

13:50.250 --> 13:54.650
<i>by abducting and releasing the PM and 
opposition leaders in a single day.</i>

13:55.010 --> 13:59.900
<i>The police call him by the code 
name, "the Phantom Solitaire,"</i>

13:59.900 --> 14:02.150
My, this is laid-back for breaking news. 
Could it be a commercial disguised as a report?

13:59.900 --> 14:03.940
<i>and he's performed feats thought 
to be humanly impossible.</i>

14:02.520 --> 14:03.940
Did he just say "Solitaire"?

14:03.940 --> 14:06.120
<i>Famed as a genius illusionist 
since childhood,</i>

14:04.490 --> 14:05.700
You know him?

14:05.700 --> 14:08.600
I've never met him, but he's famous.

14:06.120 --> 14:11.150
<i>he grew conceited and became a 
wicked discredit to the profession.</i>

14:08.630 --> 14:12.150
Almost everyone knows who he is,
at least in Japan.

14:12.870 --> 14:17.160
I've never heard of him...

14:13.110 --> 14:17.160
Oh, right. You've been trapped 
here as a ghost for five years.

14:17.570 --> 14:20.960
Like Lemmings, Solitaire's an urban 
myth that started in Shinjuku.

14:20.960 --> 14:25.260
'Course, he's been in the media too much 
to really be called a myth.

14:25.940 --> 14:29.540
Speaking of media, why did the 
person reading the news change?

14:30.010 --> 14:32.010
Hey, what channel is this?!

14:32.010 --> 14:32.220
<b>Guaranteed truth!

The legend of Ten'a Sorimura!!</b>

14:32.300 --> 14:32.970
<b>Guaranteed truth!

The legend of Ten'a Sorimura!!</b>

14:32.970 --> 14:34.970
Every channel's the same?

14:33.050 --> 14:33.720
<b>Guaranteed truth!

The legend of Ten'a Sorimura!!</b>

14:33.810 --> 14:34.970
<b>Guaranteed truth!

The legend of Ten'a Sorimura!!</b>

14:34.970 --> 14:37.600
Is this tragic news for the world?

14:37.600 --> 14:39.940
Or could it be cause for celebration?

14:39.940 --> 14:43.690
<b>Public nuisance escapes!!</b>

14:40.250 --> 14:42.080
<i>Viewers of Japan!</i>

14:42.080 --> 14:46.230
<i>Your beloved nemesis, 
Ten'a Sorimura, has returned!</i>

14:43.690 --> 14:46.230
<b>Public nuisance escapes!!</b>

14:46.230 --> 14:51.490
<b>Public nuisance escapes!!</b>

14:46.230 --> 14:51.490
<b><i>SCOOP!!</i></b>

14:46.230 --> 14:51.870
<i>Or rather, has re-debuted as the Phantom 
Solitaire! Never forget this moment!</i>

14:51.870 --> 14:57.910
<i>And to the police, who christened me,
I award a special grace period!</i>

14:58.570 --> 15:01.630
My public performances 
will resume in one week!

15:01.630 --> 15:07.000
Till then, savor your 
dull yet beautiful lives!

15:07.000 --> 15:09.180
<i>Adios? Ciao?</i>

15:09.180 --> 15:10.610
<i>Those don't feel quite right.</i>

15:10.610 --> 15:13.620
<b>I'll work on it!</b>

15:10.610 --> 15:13.620
<b>I'll work on it!</b>

15:11.040 --> 15:13.720
<i>Well, I'll work on my 
sign-off before next time.</i>

15:13.720 --> 15:15.060
<i>Good night!</i>

15:16.560 --> 15:19.350
<b>We sincerely apologize</b>

15:16.560 --> 15:21.170
<i>W-We, er, apologize for that 
disruption in our broadcast.</i>

15:19.350 --> 15:22.400
He jacked the signal?
Is there anything he <i>can't</i> do?

15:22.400 --> 15:26.070
No, I'm guessing he bought 
airtime from the Grocer.

15:26.360 --> 15:28.820
I thought the Grocer was in prison.

15:28.820 --> 15:32.820
It doesn't matter.
They don't care where they are.

15:33.890 --> 15:35.030
Come again.

15:35.580 --> 15:36.960
Oh, right.

15:36.960 --> 15:39.130
This is what makes Solitaire a problem.

15:39.130 --> 15:41.820
He's the same type of person as Lisa Kuraki.

15:41.820 --> 15:45.260
They naturally attract other troublemakers.

15:45.260 --> 15:48.750
Even ones you'd think have 
nothing to do with them.

15:49.890 --> 15:52.680
Life is full of surprises.

15:52.680 --> 15:56.120
I was in despair, thinking magic was a myth,

15:56.120 --> 15:59.930
when a new possibility was 
thrust in front of me.

16:00.620 --> 16:02.770
Wouldn't you agree,

16:02.770 --> 16:04.730
Fire-Breathing Bug?

16:02.770 --> 16:04.730
Fire
Safety

16:04.730 --> 16:06.690
<b>Fire


Safety</b>

16:06.690 --> 16:10.830
Still, I'm shocked that you answered my call.

16:12.310 --> 16:14.570
Ah, what a soothing ringtone.

16:15.030 --> 16:19.490
I may be a disgrace, but what 
magician doesn't love this tune?

16:19.870 --> 16:22.000
But, even though it's so famous,

16:22.000 --> 16:24.660
surprisingly few people know its name.

16:24.080 --> 16:25.290
Number Withheld

16:25.510 --> 16:28.290
I'm sorry, but would you wait a moment?

16:29.000 --> 16:31.720
It must be the Grocer calling to confirm.

16:31.720 --> 16:33.660
<i>"El Bimbo."</i>

16:34.640 --> 16:39.690
<i>The most famous recording is by Paul Mauriat.</i>

16:39.690 --> 16:44.640
Ah. Setting aside the question 
of how you learned this number,

16:44.960 --> 16:47.810
why would you make a phone call 
when we're standing so close?

16:48.090 --> 16:51.290
Isn't that a waste of money and bandwidth?

16:51.290 --> 16:57.800
<i>You're one to talk. You're wasting your life.</i>

16:58.200 --> 17:03.200
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

16:58.450 --> 17:03.200
<i>How did you discover me?</i>

17:04.290 --> 17:06.620
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

17:06.620 --> 17:07.210
That—

17:08.650 --> 17:12.470
Oh, my. Are you going to burn me, too?

17:12.470 --> 17:17.550
Like you burned your pitiful,
stunted imitator?

17:22.340 --> 17:26.140
Is this Ten'a Sorimura really 
such an amazing criminal?

17:26.490 --> 17:28.770
Even I know his name!

17:28.980 --> 17:32.210
Weren't there any people like 
that back in your world?

17:32.210 --> 17:35.550
You know, famous enemies of the state?

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>Aieee!</b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>Delgar, the Pirate Mayor</b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b><i>BWAH
HA
HA</i></b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>Silk, the Highborn Vampire</b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>Medion, the Rampaging Invisible Golems</b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b><i>PLOP
PLOP</i></b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>Pani, the Alchemical Scholar
of the Floating Workshop</b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>La'dial, the Slime Witch</b>

17:35.550 --> 17:40.490
<b>MUNCH
MUNCH</b>

17:36.170 --> 17:40.490
<b><i>I wanna
know more
about
Silk-san!</i></b>

17:36.320 --> 17:40.490
I never left my coal mine,
but I did still hear some rumors.

17:40.490 --> 17:44.200
For example, the Kingdom of 
Nyanild had the "King Killer,"

17:44.200 --> 17:46.540
Pirawizzo, the Venomous 
Dragon of Destruction.

17:46.540 --> 17:51.720
It fled the kingdom after a man called 
the Calamity Crusher fought it to a draw.

17:52.260 --> 17:57.050
That rumor might be what gave me the idea 
that the Calamity Crusher could kill me.

17:57.430 --> 17:59.000
The Venomous what now?

17:59.000 --> 18:00.320
Dragon of Destruction.

18:00.320 --> 18:05.140
It was only as big as a car, but it 
killed a dragon emperor worm with ease.

18:05.790 --> 18:09.560
Speaking of which, I took 
control of that worm later.

18:07.640 --> 18:09.560
<b><i>This thing</i></b>

18:07.640 --> 18:09.560
<b><i>Pirawizzo</i></b>

18:10.520 --> 18:14.570
I guess it shouldn't surprise me now,
but your world had dragons?

18:14.880 --> 18:17.090
Oh, right. This one doesn't.

18:17.090 --> 18:21.780
They're in so many stories and look so similar,
I thought you must have them.

18:22.260 --> 18:23.850
Hmm... Fascinating.

18:23.720 --> 18:25.890
Perhaps we should make 
a thorough comparison

18:25.720 --> 18:27.750
of creatures from Polka's 
world with those from our 
myths.

18:27.750 --> 18:31.710
Good idea. We might find 
other things in common.

18:32.570 --> 18:35.150
You seem to have wind and fire 
elementals, for one thing.

18:37.940 --> 18:41.590
Amazing! Like a real fire elemental!

18:41.590 --> 18:43.720
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

18:42.600 --> 18:47.390
Honestly, would it kill 
you to just hear me out?

18:47.390 --> 18:50.230
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

18:48.210 --> 18:50.990
<i>What do you mean?</i>

18:52.930 --> 18:54.920
What do I mean?

18:56.440 --> 18:57.370
A foolish question!

18:59.590 --> 19:02.160
I'm just wasting my breath, of course.

19:03.200 --> 19:07.120
I asked if you were wasting 
bandwidth earlier,

19:07.120 --> 19:09.250
but I didn't mean to criticize you!

19:09.250 --> 19:10.750
Because I

19:11.130 --> 19:13.710
adore the concept of waste!

19:14.250 --> 19:17.710
The trick to enjoying life is to enjoy waste!

19:17.710 --> 19:18.920
Wasted time!

19:18.920 --> 19:20.130
Wasted effort!

19:20.130 --> 19:21.840
Wasted money!

19:24.800 --> 19:26.730
Get rid of waste, and ultimately

19:26.730 --> 19:32.340
you become a machine that does 
nothing but breathe, eat, and sleep.

19:32.340 --> 19:38.000
To simply go on living, aren't 
human emotions themselves a waste?

19:37.980 --> 19:40.530
<b>Number Withheld</b>

19:38.650 --> 19:40.530
<i>A specious argument.</i>

19:42.410 --> 19:44.840
<i>It's nonsense.</i>

19:45.780 --> 19:54.250
Fire
Safety

19:46.280 --> 19:53.350
<i>Simply continuing to live
includes joy and pain.</i>

19:54.250 --> 19:57.750
<i>Emotions are not a bug.</i>

19:57.750 --> 20:02.510
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

19:57.750 --> 20:02.510
<i>They're a system built into life.</i>

20:02.510 --> 20:03.440
Exactly!

20:03.440 --> 20:05.340
Or so I'll say for now!

20:06.970 --> 20:09.080
I don't have the answers,

20:09.080 --> 20:11.430
and I've never actually thought 
about the meaning of life!

20:11.430 --> 20:12.690
A specious argument?

20:12.690 --> 20:15.090
No! I'm playing with words!

20:15.090 --> 20:18.360
But you're right—it <i>is</i> nonsense!

20:18.360 --> 20:20.490
I strung plausible-sounding words together

20:20.490 --> 20:22.990
and tried to make it so 
bombastic you wouldn't notice!

20:22.990 --> 20:25.530
Well done seeing through me!

20:26.090 --> 20:28.160
<b>Number Withheld</b>

20:28.160 --> 20:29.910
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

20:28.530 --> 20:32.170
You must be wondering why 
you don't feel my weight.

20:32.750 --> 20:36.300
But this is another illusion. 
There's a trick to it.

20:36.300 --> 20:38.210
Just like your fire.

20:38.570 --> 20:43.470
I'm so disappointed that your 
powers aren't magical or psychic.

20:43.900 --> 20:47.430
<i>I'm not interested in fairy tales.</i>

20:47.430 --> 20:51.850
But what if fairy tales become reality?

20:51.850 --> 20:57.960
What if something foreign entered 
this "buggy program," as you call it?

20:57.960 --> 21:03.280
Don't you need to find out whether 
this new presence in Shinjuku

21:03.280 --> 21:05.610
is a "bug" you must eliminate?

21:05.860 --> 21:10.670
<i>What will you do, if I do decide 
it's a bug that needs to burn?</i>

21:10.670 --> 21:13.660
I'll cross that bridge when I come to it.

21:13.660 --> 21:18.630
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

21:14.050 --> 21:17.580
<i>Did you not say that you 
long for the occult?</i>

21:17.580 --> 21:18.630
It's like I said earlier...

21:19.130 --> 21:22.510
I love it when things go to waste.

21:24.190 --> 21:25.550
Anyway, man.

21:25.550 --> 21:26.850
A dragon, huh?

21:26.850 --> 21:29.600
That's an enemy of the state for sure.

21:29.600 --> 21:34.310
I bet our criminals must seem 
tame compared to guys like that.

21:34.310 --> 21:36.090
I can't be sure of that.

21:36.090 --> 21:39.940
Everything is so different 
in a world without magic.

21:40.290 --> 21:45.370
And Lemmings would have been a 
real threat, even in my homeland.

21:50.730 --> 21:53.410
That can't be Lemmings, can it?

21:53.410 --> 21:55.140
<b>SQUEEZE</b>

21:55.160 --> 21:56.410
Huh?

21:56.410 --> 21:58.170
Evening.

21:58.170 --> 22:00.170
How's it going, Polka?

22:00.170 --> 22:02.320
Huh? Um...
